     If you want to establish a connection using pppppp non-interactively (such
     as from a crontab(5) entry or an at(1) job) you should use the
     --bbaacckkggrroouunndd option.  When --bbaacckkggrroouunndd is specified, pppppp attempts to es‐
     tablish the connection immediately.  If multiple phone numbers are speci‐
     fied, each phone number will be tried once.  If the attempt fails, pppppp
     exits immediately with a non-zero exit code.  If it succeeds, then pppppp
     becomes a daemon, and returns an exit status of zero to its caller.  The
     daemon exits automatically if the connection is dropped by the remote
     system, or it receives a TERM signal.

