     onds.

     Modifying the dial delay is very useful when running pppppp in --aauuttoo mode on
     both ends of the link.  If each end has the same timeout, both ends wind
     up calling each other at the same time if the link drops and both ends
     have packets queued.  At some locations, the serial link may not be reli‐
     able, and carrier may be lost at inappropriate times.  It is possible to
     have pppppp redial should carrier be unexpectedly lost during a session.

           set reconnect timeout ntries

     This command tells pppppp to re-establish the connection _n_t_r_i_e_s times on
     loss of carrier with a pause of _t_i_m_e_o_u_t seconds before each try.  For ex‐
